  <!-- 11 FAQ -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center;">11 / FAQ</p>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Steel Warehouses</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="detail-faq">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>What information do you need to quote a steel warehouse?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              For an accurate quotation, please provide: project country/city, building dimensions (length, width, eave height), intended storage use, racking system if applicable, crane requirements, roof/wall system, insulation requirements, available drawings, and local design code if specified. If you have complete drawings or BOQ, the quotation will be more accurate.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can the warehouse be designed for pallet racking?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Yes. ZhongSai can design the warehouse layout around pallet racking systems, including selective racking, double-deep racking, VNA (very narrow aisle) systems and drive-in racking. Column grid spacing is coordinated with racking module dimensions and aisle widths to maximize storage density. Specific racking configuration requires project drawings and storage requirements.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can the building include an overhead crane?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Yes. Steel warehouses can be designed with overhead crane systems. You need to provide crane capacity, span, duty class, operating range and rail top height. Crane requirements directly influence column design, foundation reactions and overall steel tonnage, and should be confirmed at the proposal stage — adding cranes later is not recommended.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
